Message 3 : Sun Sep 11 (Goth)       :: OK this time I think I MAY have it!

Ok, Referring to the equations I was discussing with Liam and Sparhawk
about making ACprevent some of the damage inflicted (got my terminal sux).
The first equation will shave off 1% damage for every 1.0 ac points below
10.0 (the mud sees 100 ac as 10.0 and -100 ac as -10.0).  This means that
a -100 AC will shave off 20% of the damage from an attack. The equation is
this:

DAMAGE = [XdY+Z] - [0.01(XdY+Z)(10.0-AC)]

But, Sparhawk wanted it so that a high hitroll would negate the effects of
the damage reduction due to AC.  The equation I made for this is based on the
assumptions below:

1. The Dicerollfor attack is 1d20
2. Thac0 is from 20 to 0, but can go lower than 0 with modifiers.
3. The mud sees, for example, -100 AC as -10.0 AC for its calculations.
4. 2 HITROLL = -1 to Thac0

Therefore,if the following equation is true, then the above damage quation
must not be used, but rather the standard XdY+Z equation should be used.

The following equation determines if the attacker hit "hard" enough to do
full damage:

[[Thac0 - (HITROLL/2)] - [Diceroll]] < or = [AC - (1.75*|AC|)]

This means that if a player's modified attack hits an AC 1.75 times less than
the opponent/mob's AC, then they will hit trough the Armor and do full damage.

I HOPE this sort of explains things for you.  If you have any questions or
find any problems with the equations (asyou prolly will) just find me on the
mud or write meme a note or something.

